  "summary": "A Congolese dandy subculture emphasizing extravagant, mismatched European haute couture fashion as a form of cultural resistance and personal expression.",
  "description": "Features deliberately mismatched luxury European clothing items, bowler hats, canes, and accessories worn with pride and confidence, creating a visual spectacle of sartorial excess. Emerged during colonial times as a form of peaceful resistance and cultural assertion, evolving into a recognized cultural movement with its own codes and aesthetics.",
